# Zoom-aware segmented hex radial

When holding on a hex to bring up the radial in edit mode, there is currently a slight delay, since drag moves the screen.'
However, screen moving is only the case in zoomed in mode. In zoomed out mode, the radial should appear immediately from the first moment of holding.
Also, instead of circles, make the radial a ring surrounding the hex split into 7 even sections, each with the appropriate colour and symbol.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] Overview edit mode opens the radial immediately on touch-down.
- [x] Detail edit mode retains the approximately 0.3-second stationary hold so an immediate drag pans.
- [x] Terrain selection is a contiguous ring around the hex with seven equal segments.
- [x] Every terrain segment uses its corresponding colour and symbol.
- [x] Number selection uses the same ring treatment with one equal segment per existing number/remove choice.
- [x] Dragging highlights the segment under the held touch and release applies only that segment.
- [x] Releasing over the centre hex or outside the ring cancels without applying.
- [x] Ring geometry and zoom-dependent timing regression coverage compile.
- [ ] Focused gesture and rendering checks pass on a functioning simulator or device.

## Implementation notes

- `BoardHexEditGestureTiming` selects a zero-duration Overview hold and the existing 0.3-second Detail hold.
- `RingSegment` draws contiguous annular wedges centred on the existing top-first option ordering.
- Terrain uses seven wedges; Number uses the same presentation with its ten tokens plus Remove.
- Shared inner/outer radii drive drawing and domain hit-testing so the centre hex and exterior remain cancellation zones.

## Evidence

- Added exact centre-index coverage for all seven terrain wedges and all eleven number/remove wedges.
- Added timing coverage for Overview and Detail, plus centre, inner-gap, and exterior cancellation coverage.
- Existing UI regression coverage continues to exercise centre release and drag-to-Brick application against the new ring radius.
- `xcodebuild build-for-testing` compiled the app, unit tests, and UI tests using `/private/tmp/Catanalyst-task031-derived`.
- Live visual and gesture verification remains intentionally deferred.
